final.rationale:
The base is Plan 3: its web first order and its single additive payload revision avoid the most conflicts and deliver value early. I grafted five things onto it.

(1) From Plan 1:
- the strict deploy compatibility rules;
- the table driven permission test for the dispatcher refactor;
- the fail closed reveal;
- the forged header tests for ACC-07;
- the rule that nothing safe waits on a decision. Because of that rule, BIZ-06 and CFG-02, which need no decision, are split from BIZ-07, which starts real messages.

(2) From Plan 2:
- balances and usage are read from billing_periods and allowance_buckets, never zella_billing_overview, which inserts a period;
- pack grants go through callerClient;
- the formatDate fallback lives in copy/labels.js, not ownerFormat.js;
- a tests/admin_detail isolated database suite with seeded fixtures;
- a pure readinessRows mapper;
- the MFA reset audits fail closed before deleteFactor;
- the resend cooldown is an atomic claim on invited_at;
- a new web app turns 'Unknown action' into 'Not available yet'.

(3) The security part of the payload change (one permission helper, activity gated on audit.view, caller numbers masked by default) is its own small PR 4, before the payload is widened in PR 9. Last sign in and two step status are returned only to callers with businesses.manage until the owner decides on BIZ-22.

(4) Readiness v2 and activation report v2 are deferred until the owner decides on them, instead of being folded into the go live migration.

(5) The to_number fix on the live call path is deferred.

Item accounting. Items whose server half and UI half ship separately are labelled by part: (data) and (UI), or (part a), (part b) and so on. Each part appears in exactly one PR or in deferred, and all 29 still true items are covered.

Overlap with the Businesses list job (the shared files are OwnerDashboard.jsx, index.ts, settings.ts and ownerFormat.js):
- PRs 2, 4, 5 and 8 touch OwnerDashboard.jsx (readRoute and the BusinessDetails props block) or the index.ts dispatcher check (about lines 3077 to 3088). They merge after the list PR and rebase onto origin/main.
- This page reuses that job's hasPermission helper and its `me` prop. If the list job ships no server side helper, PR 4 adds adminPermissions() to settings.ts and the list job reuses it.
- In ownerFormat.js, this work only replaces ACTION_LABELS with a re-export (PR 1). It never touches businessState, STAGE_LABELS or 'ready' (BIZ-27).
- New settings.ts PERMISSIONS keys are appended at the end, one per line.
- index.ts edits stay out of dashboard_data and the new paged list action.
- After PR 2, each later PR edits its own tab file, not the monolith.

Deploy rules. Production runs edge v18 and the old web app.
- Every edge change only adds fields. Activity becomes [] plus activityAllowed:false, never null. The calls array is masked first and removed only in PR 19, after PR 3's web app is live.
- New actions ship before the web app that calls them, and the web app degrades if they are missing.
- SQL ships before the edge code that needs it. Each migration behaves exactly like today when its new input is absent.
- No migration here replaces zella_set_business_size or zella_business_readiness, so sql/zella_admin_permissions.sql's md5 guards still hold.
- Suggested edge deploy windows, each needing approval:
  - A: PRs 4, 6, 7, 8 and 9;
  - B: PRs 12 and 13 (13 knowing that turning on an automation for a live business starts real messages);
  - after that, each decision gated action PR on its own (14 to 18);
  - PR 19 once PR 3 is live.
- Web only PRs (1, 2, 3, 5, 10, 11) need no edge approval.

Tests. All database tests run only in the isolated database (zprod3 through tests/security/zpsql.sh with isolated_guard.sh). zprod3 has no platform_role_permissions rows and no calls, so each suite seeds its own fixtures and never uses customer data. The other test layers are deno *_test.ts inside owner-provision-business, node --test web units, and the local browser harness (tests/browser with local-backend.mjs). Real email, MFA resets, pack grants, calls and go live are stubbed and never run on production without approval for that specific action.

Every PR updates docs/PRODUCT.md, and docs/MEMORY.md when what is live changes. Migrations also regenerate BACKEND_SCHEMA.md and update SCHEMA_STATUS.md after they are applied.

prs.tests:
Isolated database (tests/admin_detail), with a seeded business that has a plan, an open period, buckets including a pack and a rollover, a number, open and resolved alerts, and deliveries (served, not_ready with problems, unknown_number):
- each RPC is callable as the service role;
- the billing_periods row count is unchanged after a detail read;
- summed usage equals zella_billing_overview's numbers for the same business, called as a billing.view admin.
Deno:
- prices are stripped without billing.view;
- a period that is missing or expired;
- resolved alerts are ignored;
- routingFrom matches zella_admin_routing_get output on fixtures;
- the deliveries payload has no caller number.

